# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# splash: on
# The screen the desktop comes up behind.
#
# Black over everything, the mark in the middle of it, and one line under
# the mark naming the part of the system that has just been built.  The
# stages are held during startup, before this script's loop begins, so
# what a script can see is the LAST of them and the way out; the
# arithmetic that paces the rest is test_splash's to hold.
#
# The three probes below come first and together, because everything they
# look at is on its way out: spending script turns on notes between them
# is spending the hold they are inside of.
wait 1
expect-pixel 5 5 000000
expect-pixel 507 307 f7e689
expect-pixel 466 398 dcdcdc
note black to the corner, so it covers the screen rather than a panel in
note the middle of one; the mark on it in its own colours, pinned on the
note filled face, which is the largest steady area it has; and the line
note naming the stage under it -- on a stroke of the text rather than
note with expect-ink, which asks only that a pixel is not WHITE and so
note would pass on a black screen without looking at anything
wait 150
expect-pixel 5 5 336698
expect-pixel 500 315 d8d8d8
note and then the black is LIFTED off the desktop rather than replaced by
note it: the backdrop at that same corner, and the panel of a window
note where the mark was standing
quit
